If I keep `@dataclass`, it will generate `__eq__` and `__hash__ = None` (unless `frozen=True`).
If I define my own `__eq__`, the dataclass generated `__eq__` is overridden.
If I define my own `__hash__`, it overrides `__hash__ = None`.

But actually, if I'm implementing `__eq__` and `__hash__` myself, do I even need `@dataclass`?
`@dataclass` provides `__init__`, `__repr__`, etc. I probably want to keep those.

